{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSemisimpleGeneral","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimple","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.finrank_traceQuot_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.finrank_traceQuot_pos","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalSemisimple.lean#L169-L184","doc":"**The dimension is strictly positive** — the equation above is not `0 = 0`.\n\n`finrank_traceQuot` is an equation between two things that could in principle both vanish, and\n`AlgEquiv.ofBijective` upstream would have accepted a bijection of one-point algebras.  This\nforecloses that reading by reusing `traceQuot_one_ne_zero`: the class of `1` differs from the\nclass of `0`, so the quotient is `Nontrivial`, and it is finite-dimensional by transport, so its\n`finrank` is positive.  Hence the two-row sum of squares is nonzero as well. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.finrank_traceQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.finrank_traceQuot","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalSemisimple.lean#L148-L167","doc":"**The dimension of the quotient is the two-row sum of squares.**\n\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ n+1, ℓ(λ) ≤ 2} (f^λ)²`, where `f^λ = card (StandardYoungTableau λ)`.  This is the one\nstatement in this file that is genuinely downstream of `traceQuotEquiv` rather than of the\nolder `heckeWedderburn`: the *restriction of the index set* to at-most-two rows is what the\nradical identification buys, and the dimension is where that restriction becomes a number.\n\n🛑 This is **not** `= catalan (n+1)`, and not a `TL_n(δ)` identification.  See the module\ndocstring for both gaps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.isSemisimpleRing_traceQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.isSemisimpleRing_traceQuot","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalSemisimple.lean#L136-L146","doc":"**`H_n(q) / rad(wtrace)` is semisimple, for every `n`, at convention D.**\n\n🛑 Not new — see this file's module docstring: routes (1) and (2) reach it without\n`traceQuotEquiv` at all, and route (1) is general over any `CharZero` field.  Written via the\nequivalence only because that is one line.  Do not cite `traceQuotEquiv` as the reason this\nholds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.isSemisimpleRing_traceQuot_of_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.isSemisimpleRing_traceQuot_of_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalSemisimple.lean#L118-L134","doc":"**Semisimplicity by the route that does NOT use `traceQuotEquiv`** — a quotient of a\nsemisimple ring is semisimple.\n\nThis proves, rather than asserts, route (1) of the module docstring, and it is the honest\nstatement of where this fact comes from.  Note the hypotheses: **`hq0` and `hq2` only.**  The\nequivalence route below additionally needs `hq21` and `hgen`, the latter strictly stronger than\n`hq2` — so this route is not merely independent of `traceQuotEquiv`, it is *sharper*.\n\n`RingCon.mk'` is the quotient map and is surjective by `Quot.exists_rep`; the semisimplicity of\nthe numerator is `isSemisimpleRing_hecke_generic`, which holds over any `CharZero` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRingTwoRowBlocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRingTwoRowBlocks","kind":"instance","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalSemisimple.lean#L113-L116","doc":"**The target is semisimple.**  A finite product of matrix algebras over a division ring:\nMathlib's finite-product instance over this corpus's `instIsSemisimpleRing_matrix`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.instFiniteTwoRowIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple.instFiniteTwoRowIdx","kind":"instance","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalSemisimple.lean#L108-L111","doc":"The at-most-two-row index set is finite — a subtype of `Nat.Partition (n+1)`, which\nMathlib gives as a `Fintype`.  Stated via `Subtype.finite` so that no decidability of the\nrow-length predicate is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}